### Describe the bug

If an async method of a class is using the `arguments` object, the reference to the object is lost.

I have a reproduction here https://github.com/egilsster/swc-jest-issue/blob/main/src/args.test.ts

This starts to work with `target` set to `es2018`

Related to https://github.com/swc-project/swc/issues/2786

### Input code

```typescript
export class Quirk {
  async doStuff() {
    const args = arguments;
    console.log(args);
    return { foo: null, ...args[0] };
  }
}
```

```typescript
const args = { one: 1, two: 2 };
const quirk = new Quirk();
// @ts-ignore using old js syntax
const res = await quirk.doStuff(args);
```

### Config

```json
{
  "jsc": {
    "target": "es2015",
    "parser": {
      "syntax": "typescript"
    }
  },
  "sourceMaps": true,
  "inlineSourcesContent": true
}
```


### Playground link

_No response_

### Expected behavior

I expect the `arguments` object to be `{ '0': { one: 1, two: 2 } }` in my case.

### Version

1.2.112

